          "lineage": "Haplopoma",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "<p>Haplopoma sciaphilum is an encrusting bryozoan that forms small patch-like colonies. Colonies are typically composed of 10-25 autozooids, occasionally reaching 50 autozooids. Autozooids are elongate, oval to hexagonal. They are 0.5-0.55 by 0.26-0.29 mm.</p>",
